SF Survival is a standalone ShroudForge mod with eight optional survival settings. Its package ID is <code>sf-survival</code>. It targets the client and Dedicated Server and uses the public typed runtime API. The package is disabled by default and has no dependency on SF Unlimited Flight.

{| class="wikitable"
! Setting !! Effect !! Engine value or scope
|-
| No Fall Damage || Turns off fall damage. || Adjusts <code>fallDamageStartDistance</code> on the player character template, keeping it at least as high as the lethal distance.
|-
| Fast Health Regen || Multiplies existing health regeneration by up to 100. || Uses existing <code>Health_Recharge</code>, capped at 65,536. Requires natural health regeneration.
|-
| Fast Mana Regen || Multiplies existing mana regeneration by up to 100. || Uses existing <code>Mana_Recharge</code>, capped at 65,536. Requires natural mana regeneration.
|-
| Infinite Stamina || Keeps stamina at its current maximum. || Updates the original stamina bounds when the maximum changes. It does not periodically refill the current value.
|-
| Infinite Underwater Breath || Keeps the underwater breath reserve at its current maximum. || Uses the original oxygen attribute bounds.
|-
| Infinite Weapon Durability || Disables durability loss for the hosted world. || Changes the world-level <code>enableDurability</code> setting. Other players' items are affected too.
|-
| Infinite Frost Timer || Keeps body warmth at its current maximum. || Uses the original body-heat attribute bounds.
