== How the effects work ==

Attribute effects are applied to authoritative player entities. Infinite Stamina, Infinite Mana, and Infinite Underwater Breath change the relevant minimum bound to match the current maximum. The game's own attribute calculation continues to consume and clamp the value. When a maximum changes, the mod checks and updates the related bounds together.

Fast regeneration multiplies the game's existing regeneration value. It retains the original timeout and ramp. It does not create a separate regeneration event, and it has no effect if natural regeneration is disabled.

Fall-damage configuration belongs to the shared player template, so players using that template share the change. Weapon durability is a world-wide setting and affects every player in the hosted world, including other players' carried items.

== Turning settings off and restoration ==

The mod remembers every original value it changes. When a setting is disabled or the mod unloads during the same world session, it restores the original input. Before writing, it checks that the current value is still the value owned by the mod. If another system changed it, that external change is preserved.

If an engine gate is busy, restoration is retried on a later update. An uncertain write stops further mutation. If cleanup cannot finish while the mod is being disabled, the runtime retains the scope and retries cleanup. Package refresh is aborted if cleanup cannot complete.

Turn settings off before leaving the world and wait for restoration. An invalidated world session cannot authorize writes to old shared storage. If that happens while shared settings are still owned, the mod stops and reports that a game restart is needed.

